# Copy this file to scope.txt and fill in domains you have written
# authorization to test:
#   cp scope.txt.example scope.txt
#
# scope.txt itself is git-ignored — it may reflect a private program's
# scope, so don't commit your real one.
#
# Format: one pattern per line.
#   *.example.com    -> matches example.com AND any subdomain of it
#   example.com      -> matches only that exact host, not subdomains
#   !internal.example.com  -> explicit exclusion, wins over any match above it
#
# If scope.txt doesn't exist, the script will offer to create one
# automatically (pre-filled with the domain you type in) on first run —
# but for real engagements, fill this in yourself from the program's
# official scope definition rather than relying on that shortcut.

*.example.com
example.com
!internal.example.com
